  "content": {
    "title": "What World Cup qualifiers are today? FIFA and UEFA playoff schedule",
    "text": "March 26, 2026, 9:59 a.m. ETThe final six World Cup places will be decided in playoffs across the globe in the coming days.Thursday, March 26 is a huge day in World Cup qualifying, with eight semifinals in European playoffs and two in an intercontinental playoff. The winners of those matches will advance to finals on Tuesday, March 31, where World Cup spots will be on the line.In Europe, 16 teams have qualified for a playoff and are divided in four paths of four teams each. One team will emerge from each path and advance to the World Cup.Meanwhile, two World Cup spots are on the line in Mexico as FIFA holds its intercontinental playoffs.Six teams will play in playoffs: one from South America (Bolivia), one from Oceania (New Caledonia), one from Asia (Iraq), one from Africa (DR Congo), and two from Concacaf (Jamaica and Suriname).Below is the full match schedule for FIFA World Cup playoffs on Thursday, March 26.FIFA World Cup playoff scheduleUEFA World Cup playoffPath ASF1: Italy vs Northern Ireland - March 26, Bergamo, Italy, 3:45 p.m. ETSF2: Wales vs Bosnia and Herzegovina - March 26, Cardiff, Wales, 3:45 p.m. ETPath BSF3: Ukraine vs Sweden - March 26, Valencia, Spain, 3:45 p.m. ETSF4: Poland vs Albania - March 26, Warsaw, Poland, 3:45 p.m. ETPath CSF5: Turkey vs Romania - March 26, Istanbul, Turkey, 1 p.m. ETSF6: Slovakia vs Kosovo - March 26, Bratislava, Slovakia, 3:45 p.m. ETPath DSF7: Denmark vs North Macedonia - March 26, Copenhagen, Denmark, 3:45 p.m. ETSF8: Czechia vs Ireland - March 26, Prague, Czechia, 3:45 p.m. ETWhich teams are qualified for 2026 World Cup?FIFA intercontinental playoffBolivia vs. Suriname - March 26, Monterrey, Mexico, 6 p.m. ETNew Caledonia vs. Jamaica - March 26, Guadalajara, Mexico, 11 p.m. ETHow to watch World Cup qualifying playoffsAll eight European playoff matches on Thursday, March 26 will stream live on ViX, while FS2 will broadcast Turkey vs. Romania and Poland vs. Albania, with FS1 showing Wales vs. Bosnia and Herzegovina.FS1 will carry both intercontinental playoff matches on Thursday.Watch World Cup playoffs on Fubo Watch European World Cup playoffs on Prime VideoOur team of savvy editors independently handpicks all recommendations. If you purchase through our links, the USA TODAY Network may earn a commission. Prices were accurate at the time of publication but may change.",
